# OVER: the WALKABLE PIPE's test course (SPEC.md 137.12.3.7) - not shipped, on no disk, in no tour: compiled by
# `bbcourse.py --selfcheck`'s section `pipeover` and by tests/bonanza_phys.py's crossing scenes (the guest's archway
# part against the model).  A CROSSING: one KEEP tube along row 12 with `top`, its two end legs walls one unit over
# the floor and its middle leg (x 10 - 16) a pipe hanging `column 1` deep, two units over the floor - so the ball
# rolls UNDER it (the lower path, down column 13) and, with `top`, ALONG it (the upper path):
#   the upper path: the start on the north tier (5 units, the pipe's top), south onto the pipe, east along its top
#                   over column 13, south off it onto the south tier and down to the floor
#   the lower path: down column 13 on the floor, under the pipe
# Each end leg's top is a floor too (3 units): the ball rolls off the pipe's top onto it.
course OVER "Pipe crossing"
